---
/**
 * `/data-terms` — the URL every published Optfall payload carries.
 *
 * `docs/DATA-TERMS.md` has each dataset embed
 * `"terms": "https://optfall.com/data-terms"`, and until this page existed that
 * link 404'd. A terms URL that does not resolve is worse than none: it is a
 * claim of provenance a recipient cannot check, on a project whose whole thesis
 * is being right.
 *
 * The page is deliberately a SUMMARY that points at the canonical document
 * rather than a second copy of it. Two prose copies of a licensing position
 * drift, and the one people would find first is the one nobody edits. The
 * disclaimer is the exception — it is required verbatim in the footer of every
 * page, which `scripts/check-disclaimer.ts` enforces against the built output.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const CANONICAL =
  "https://github.com/alxjrvs/optfall/blob/main/docs/DATA-TERMS.md";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Data terms — Optfall"
  description="Terms on the data Optfall publishes: what is openly licensed, and what belongs to Legend Story Studios."
>
  <h1>Data terms</h1>

  <p>
    This page summarises the terms on data Optfall publishes. The canonical text is <a href={CANONICAL}><code>docs/DATA-TERMS.md</code></a>, and where the two differ, that document governs.
  </p>

  <h2>What is openly licensed</h2>

  <p>
    The <strong>structural work this project owns</strong>: rule identifiers, the legality timeline, version diffs, and annotations. These are ours to license, and they are published openly so that if this site disappears the corpus does not.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not ours to license</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>Card names, card text and card art remain the property of Legend Story Studios</strong> and are never relicensed here. Optfall uses them under LSS's published policy for third-party applications, which permits card databases and rules-enforcement tools on conditions that bind anyone we pass the data to as well.
  </p>

  <p>
    So a dataset from Optfall carries two things at once: an open licence over the structure, and LSS's conditions over the game content inside it. Redistributing one without the other is not something this project can authorise.
  </p>

  <h2>The copyright line, and why no card faces are shown</h2>

  <!--
    THIS SECTION USED TO DESCRIBE A COMPONENT THAT DOES NOT EXIST. It said the
    copyright notice "is rendered by the component itself rather than passed
    in, so it cannot be omitted" — which is the *contract*
    (`CARD_IMAGE_COPYRIGHT` and `CardImageProps` in
    `packages/components/src/index.ts`), not an implementation: there is no
    `CardImage.svelte`. A compliance page asserting a guarantee that is only
    prose is the exact failure the rest of this site is built to avoid, so it
    now says what is true, and the card pages render no faces at all.

    Inline elements stay on the same source line as the text around them: the
    build compresses this HTML and drops the whitespace at a line break falling
    immediately before an inline tag.
  -->
  <p>
    Wherever card images are shown, the notice <code>© Legend Story Studios</code> must accompany them. <strong>Optfall shows no card faces today.</strong> The component contract that would carry that notice exists — it is deliberately not a prop, so a caller cannot omit or empty it — but the component itself is not built, and rather than write a bare image tag that satisfies neither the contract nor the condition, the card pages cite each printing by its collector number, set and artist and show no artwork.
  </p>

  <h2>The card data</h2>

  <p>
    The card corpus Optfall publishes is a trimmed, commit-pinned copy of an actively maintained community dataset, and it carries its own rights notice inside the file. Only Optfall's structural work over it — the field selection, the upstream pin, the derived legality verdicts and this envelope — is openly licensed. The card names and card text inside it are Legend Story Studios' and are not relicensed by us or by anyone we pass the file to.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
